 Buzzing Stocks: Leela Palaces Hotels & Resorts rises 5% after brokerages keep ‘Buy’; IDBI Bank falls 5% on stake sale developments
 IDBI Bank share price fell 5% after Fairfax Financial Holdings-backed Canada Inc has been approved as the strategic buyer of IDBI Bank, with the government and Life Insurance Corporation of India (LIC) set to divest a combined 60.72% stake for Rs 52,878 crore. 
 Moneycontrol News 
 October 15, 2026 / 11:38 IST 
 --> 
 Buzzing Stocks 
 Stock-specific activity is likely to remain in focus on Dalal Street on October 15, following a slew of corporate developments, brokerage recommendations and earnings.
Shares of Leela Palaces Hotels & Resorts added 5% after research house Jefferies maintained Buy with target price at Rs 735/share and Nomura also maintained 'buy' rating with a target price at Rs 650/share.
IDBI Bank share price fell 5% after Fairfax Financial Holdings-backed Canada Inc has been approved as the strategic buyer of IDBI Bank, with the government and Life Insurance Corporation of India (LIC) set to divest a combined 60.72% stake for Rs 52,878 crore. The government will divest a 30.48% stake in the bank, while LIC will sell its 30.24% stake. Canada Inc will acquire the shares at Rs 81 apiece. Following the transaction, the government will retain a 15% stake in IDBI Bank, while LIC will continue to hold 19%.
Share price of HDB Financial Services share price fell 4 percent even though the company reported a 34.2 percent year-on-year jump in Q2 profit to Rs 780.2 crore, while net interest income rose 15.6 percent to Rs 2,533.7 crore.
Bajaj Consumer Care share price declined 4 percent despite the company reported a 65.9 percent year-on-year surge in Q2 consolidated profit to Rs 70.2 crore, while revenue grew 25.5 percent to Rs 332.8 crore.
Ceat share price slipped more than 2 percent after the company reported a 39.8 percent year-on-year decline in Q2 consolidated profit to Rs 112 crore, despite a 26.2 percent increase in revenue to Rs 4,762 crore. The company reported an exceptional loss of Rs 13 crore, including a one-time cost related to voluntary retirement schemes.
Enviro Infra Engineers share price added 3 percent after its subsidiary, Suyog Urja, received a Letter of Intent from Arie Energy LLP for a Rs 228-crore project. The contract involves turnkey engineering, procurement and construction works for the 100 MW Ajani Wind Power Project in Latur, Maharashtra.
Shares of Om Power Transmission share price gained nearly 3 percent after the company received a Letter of Acceptance from Uttar Gujarat Vij Company for a Rs 101.56-crore turnkey contract. The project involves converting the existing electrical line network into an underground cable network, along with associated works, in Ambaji.
Investors are expected to remain focused on brokerage calls, block deals, order wins, regulatory developments and other company-specific triggers that could drive stock-level volatility during the session.
